{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>When you go to return to Egypt.</b> Every time I send you from your tent — so that you are outside the city of Egypt, as it says: כְּצֵאתִי אֶת הָעִיר אֶפְרֹשׂ כַּפַּי (Exodus 9:29) — I will command you to return to Egypt to speak to Pharaoh." "<b>See all the signs which I have placed in your hand.</b> Look each time at all the signs that are then placed in your hand, so as to perform them in the manner and order that I command you." "<b>And you shall perform them before Pharaoh.</b> Then you will succeed in performing them before Pharaoh, when you do not deviate. For when a person sins against his Creator's commandments in excess or deficiency, he corrupts the intent and it does not succeed — as was the case at the waters of Meribah. So too He commanded regarding the observance of the commandments: לֹא תֹסִפוּ וְלֹא תִגְרְעוּ (Deuteronomy 4:2)." "<b>And I will harden his heart.</b> For since he was unable to endure the plagues, he would have sent the people away without doubt — not because he would submit to the blessed Elohim to do His will. Therefore He hardened his heart, so that he would steel himself to endure the plagues and not send them away."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:25.759248951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}